From: Joan Karadimov <joan.karadimov@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Clear only the flag setFlag() is given

setFlag(f, false) masks the flags with !f, which is 0 for any flag, so
clearing one flag clears them all. Turning off BigEndian on a
little-endian stream also turns off FloatIEEE, and every readFloat()
and writeFloat() after that fails with Unsupported.

Upstream: not submitted
---
diff --git a/src/binio.cpp b/src/binio.cpp
--- a/src/binio.cpp
+++ b/src/binio.cpp
@@ -89,7 +89,7 @@
   if(set)
     my_flags |= f;
   else
-    my_flags &= !f;
+    my_flags &= ~f;
 }
 
 bool binio::getFlag(Flag f)
